(1. LEXICAL SOURCE VERBS & DEICTIC TRAJECTORIES) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Tangkhul distinguishes three basic deictic path vectors: \(i\) Centripetal) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(movement toward speaker \(-ung eina ungkaphung\), \(ii\) Centrifugal) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(movement away from speaker \(-va eina vazatkasa\), and \(iii\) Altitude-) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(conditioned vectors: ascent uphill \(-ka\) and descent downhill \(-tuk\).) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(Tangkhul Linguistic Data & Analysis:) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * ung-kaphung : to arrive coming home toward speaker) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: Centripetal motion.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * va-zatkasa : to go away departing from speaker) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: Centrifugal motion.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * thuk-kashok : to climb up out of a gorge onto peak) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: Ascending vertical vector.) Tj
0 -12 Td
